    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Soul Asylum's Let Your Dim Light Shine is a 1995 rock album that solidified the band's presence in the alternative rock scene of the 1990s. Released by Columbia Records, the album features a blend of melodic guitar-driven rock, introspective lyrics, and accessible songwriting, characteristic of the band's signature style. Musically, it expands on the sound established in their breakthrough album Grave Dancers Union, with a mix of anthemic choruses, gritty riffs, and emotional depth, while also exploring more polished production and varied arrangements.\n\nAs the follow-up to their commercial peak, Let Your Dim Light Shine marked a pivotal moment in Soul Asylum's discography. It included the hit single \"Misery,\" which became a staple on rock radio and helped the album achieve platinum status. While critics noted a shift toward a more mainstream sound compared to their earlier work, the album was generally well-received for its consistency and songcraft. Commercially, it performed strongly, further cementing Soul Asylum's reputation as one of the leading alternative rock acts of the era.",
